## Separate problems and tickets

### Parser: month-first interpretation in a day-first tenant

The shared parser reads dates month first. A day-first tenant's intended 7 April can become 4 July.
This affects app and email intake, plus forms that do not take the booking-v3 hint path.
Classify using the tenant's configured locale and the actual channel, not the reporter's browser locale.

[Parser issue #2 and report membership](https://github.com/piotter121/mega-challange-s01e03/issues/2).
Reproduce with an ambiguous date, then verify the intended date survives parsing, storage, invite and reminder.
Include a date whose day exceeds twelve to check rejection/validation rather than a silent swap.

### Hint: booking-v3 tells day-first users to enter month first

The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` while interpreting input according to the day-first tenant locale.
The hint encourages an input order that the form then reads differently. The affected form tenants are
`alder.physio`, `copper.studio` and `pale.harbour`; their app/email reports still take the parser path.

[Hint issue #1 and report membership](https://github.com/piotter121/mega-challange-s01e03/issues/1).
Make the displayed hint, validation and interpretation agree. Test each affected tenant on booking-v3,
and check booking-v2 plus month-first locale controls. A parser-only change does not establish that the hint is fixed.

The following original component shows the exported desk state. Its “no ticket of its own” label
describes that snapshot; the links above identify the separate GitHub tickets created by this review.

